// The repository holds two Go modules that are deliberately separate:
// `entrypoint` ships inside the image, `test/e2e` drives it from outside
// and must never add a dependency to it. This workspace exists only so
// editors, gopls and repo-root commands (`go vet ./entrypoint/...
// ./test/e2e/...`) see both at once without an editor reconfiguration
// per directory.
//
// It is invisible to the image build: the Dockerfile's gobuild stage
// COPYs `entrypoint/` alone, so this file is not in its context and the
// in-image build keeps resolving the entrypoint module on its own.
go 1.24.0

use (
	./entrypoint
	./test/e2e
)
